SEO plan of attack. Reasoning and sources are in SEO.md.

Decisions: international English, Josh writes the copy, no articles.
Order matters. Phase 1 aims everything else, so do not skip it.

    Phase 1 - Aim before building (you):
        ✔ Search Console: export last 3 months of the Performance report @done(26-10-22)
        ✔ Read the queries, pages, countries and devices reports @done(26-10-22)
        ✔ Reversed the UK leaning decision, the audience is international @done(26-10-22)
            - UK is 18% of impressions and the worst CTR of the top countries
            - Findings written up in SEO.md under "What the data actually said"

        Target terms, in priority order:
            - volleyball scoreboard            95 imp, position 18.0, 0 clicks
            - volleyball scoreboard online    110 imp, position 11.2, 10 clicks
            - online volleyball scoreboard     41 imp, position 13.8, 2 clicks
            - volleyball scoreboards           67 imp, position 28.3, 0 clicks
            - volleyball score online          38 imp, position 24.9, 0 clicks
            - scoreboard volleyball            36 imp, position 19.4, 0 clicks

    Phase 2 - Technical, no copy needed (me):
        ✔ Make the homepage h1 descriptive @done(26-10-22)
            - h1 is sr-only so the wordmark stays the hero visually
        ✔ Noindex /match and drop it from the sitemap @done(26-10-22)
            - Verified: serves "noindex, follow", sitemap is down to / and the
              manifest. /basic-match impressions will fall away with it.
        ✔ Confirm the homepage still server-renders its text @done(26-10-22)
            - 200 chars and the h1 both present in the raw HTML

    Phase 3 - Page structure (me):
        ✔ Homepage copy lives in lib/homepage-content.ts @done(26-10-23)
        ✔ Content sits behind a closed disclosure at the foot of the page @done(26-10-23)
            - Native <details>, not the Radix Collapsible, which unmounts its
              content and would keep the text out of the HTML entirely
            - Google's spam policy, updated May 2026, lists accordions as a
              legitimate pattern and collapsed text gets full ranking weight
            - Always shown, not conditional, so nothing shifts after hydration
        ✔ Cut the scoring rules section @done(26-10-23)
            - It targets a different topic from "volleyball scoreboard", which
              is the only thing the data shows demand for. Chasing rules
              queries would be the article writing that was ruled out.
        ✔ Structure above the fold left exactly as it was @done(26-10-23)

    Phase 4 - Copy (you):
        ✔ Approved, with the target phrases worked into prose @done(26-10-23)
        ✔ Title tag now leads with "Free", matching how people search @done(26-10-23)
            - Carried through to the open graph and twitter titles
        ☐ Optional later: make the disclosure read more obviously clickable
            - Label is a description rather than an action
            - A full width row would be more recognisable than centred text

    Phase 5 - Ship and verify:
        ✔ Verified in the rendered HTML: title, three headings, 881 chars, @done(26-10-23)
          disclosure closed, target phrases x3 each
        ☐ Push and deploy (me)
        ☐ Search Console: request reindex of / and resubmit the sitemap (you)
        ☐ Wait. Indexing is days, position movement is weeks.

    Phase 6 - Measure (me):
        ☐ PageSpeed Insights on / and /match, record the field data
            - Targets: LCP under 2.5s, INP under 200ms, CLS under 0.1
            - INP matters most here: every point tapped is a store update, a
              re-render and a localStorage write
            - Fix only what actually fails
        ☐ Re-read Search Console 4-6 weeks after deploy, compare to Phase 1

    Optional, low value:
        ☐ FAQPage structured data on the scoring section
            - Rich results were removed on 7 May 2026, so there is no search
              result from this any more. Google still reads it for page
              understanding. Only worth adding if it is nearly free.
        ☐ Look at why desktop ranks at 22.9 against mobile at 9.7
            - Noticed in the Phase 1 export, cause unknown, may be nothing

    Explicitly not doing:
        ☐ llms.txt - no measurable effect, Google confirmed nothing reads it
        ☐ More meta tag work - already done well, no return left
        ☐ Explainer articles - decided against

    Competitive gaps, product work not SEO, recorded so they are not lost:
        ☐ Live sync across devices
        ☐ Share a view link or QR code to spectators
        ☐ TV display mode
